### Swap Architecture

```text
Traditional Swap:

Partition
   ↓
mkswap
   ↓
swap
   ↓
/etc/fstab
   ↓
swapon


LVM Swap:

Disk/Partition
   ↓
PV
   ↓
VG
   ↓
LV
   ↓
mkswap
   ↓
swap
   ↓
/etc/fstab
   ↓
swapon
```

### LVM Storage Model

```text
Physical Disk
      ↓
Physical Volume
      ↓
Volume Group
      ↓
Physical Extents
      ↓
Logical Volume
      ↓
Filesystem or Swap
```

The Volume Group acts as the storage pool, allowing Logical Volumes to consume available Physical Extents from the PVs that belong to that VG.
